{{Quote|Admiral, we have the plans!|Shollan|audio=Shollan-Plans.flac|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
[[Lieutenant]] '''Shollan''' was a [[Mon Calamari]] [[Gender|male]] who served under [[Admiral]] [[Raddus]] in the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]]. [[Homeworld|Hailing]] from the [[waterworld]] of [[Mon Cala]], he and fellow Mon Calamari [[Caitken]] were [[aide]]s to Raddus, and in [[1 BBY]], the three attended a briefing where the possibility of an [[Battle of Scarif|attack]] on the [[planet]] [[Scarif]] to steal the [[Death Star plans]] was discussed. When the mission was carried out by a [[Rogue One|group]] of rogue rebels, Raddus joined their attack onboard his [[flagship]], the ''[[Profundity]]'', with Shollan and Caitken by his side.

At Scarif, Shollan gave Raddus several updates throughout the battle. In the course of the fight, the ''Profundity'' was able to destroy the [[Shield Gate]] at the instructions of former [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[pilot]] [[Bodhi Rook]], who was on the surface, at which point Shollan excitedly reported to Raddus that they were receiving a transmission from Scarif. The [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]], whose plans they had stolen, then emerged from hyperspace, so Raddus called for the [[fleet]] to jump to [[hyperspace]]; however, the ''Profundity'' was disabled by an [[Devastator|''Imperial''-class Star Destroyer]], and most of the crew aboard it perished.

==Biography==
===Aide to the admiral===
{{Quote|I say we fight!|Raddus, while standing in front of Shollan|audio=Raddus-Fight.flac|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
[[File:White_Calamari.png|thumb|left|250px|Caitken (left) and Shollan (right) served as aides to Admiral Raddus.]]
Shollan [[Homeworld|hailed]] from the [[waterworld]] of [[Mon Cala]] on the [[planet]]'s colder polar regions.<ref name="UVG" /> He<ref name="Topps" /> served as a [[lieutenant]]<ref name="Art">''[[Art of Coloring: Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> and [[Communications officer|comms officer]]<ref name="Novel" /> in the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]].<ref name="Rogue One" /> Alongside fellow [[Mon Calamari]] [[Caitken]], Shollan was an [[aide]] to [[Admiral]] [[Raddus]]<ref name="UVG" /> and, between [[4 BBY]] and [[3 BBY]],<ref name="Date 3BBY">In ''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]'', the report from Caitken and Shollan is set between the [[blockade of Ibaar]] and the [[Mission to Ryloth (Phoenix Squadron)|mission to Ryloth]], which ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' respectively dates to [[4 BBY]] and [[3 BBY]].</ref> they put together a report on the status of the [[Rebel Alliance Navy|Alliance Fleet]] [[starship]]s, which Raddus then forwarded to Alliance leader [[Mon Mothma]].<ref name="TRF">''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]''</ref> In [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Date 1BBY" /> Shollan and Caitken stood next to Raddus during a meeting in Alliance [[Great Temple|headquarters]] on<ref name="Rogue One" /> the [[moon]]<ref name="UVG" /> [[Yavin 4]], in which [[Alliance High Command]] discussed whether or not the intel from the recently [[Liberation of Erso|rescued]] rebel [[Jyn Erso]] on the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] [[superweapon]] was accurate. However, without the full support of the council, an attack would not be authorized.<ref name="Rogue One" />

Nonetheless, Erso, along with many other rebels, commandeered a [[SW-0608|''Zeta''-class Heavy Cargo Shuttle]] that they had [[Mission to Eadu|stolen]] from the Empire, intending to go to the planet [[Scarif]] to [[Thief|steal]] the [[Death Star plans]] themselves.<ref name="Rogue One" /> A rebel [[soldier]] informed Raddus of this move, who agreed with it. With Shollan and Caitken at his side, he ordered that his [[flagship]], the [[MC75 Star Cruiser]] ''[[Profundity]]'', be made ready for departure, and it quickly was. The [[fleet]] then jumped into [[hyperspace]] to join the rogue rebels, [[Rogue One]].<ref name="RO5">[[Rogue One Adaptation 5|''Rogue One Adaptation'' 5]]</ref>

===Battle of Scarif===
{{Quote|What's going on down there, lieutenant?''"<br />"''Unknown, sir. We can't raise them. All rebel frequencies are blocked.|Raddus and Shollan|audio=Raddus-Shollan-Blocked.flac|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
[[File:MonCalamariTrio-RO.png|thumb|right|300px|Shollan, Raddus, and Caitken on the ''Profundity'']]
The fleet arrived at Scarif, and Raddus ordered the [[Squad leader|squadron leaders]] where to take their [[starfighter]]s as Shollan and Caitken interacted with devices affixed to their chairs. As the battle progressed, Raddus asked Shollan what was occurring below them inside the [[Shield Gate]]. However, Shollan reported that that information was unknown and that they had tried to raise the rebels there, but all rebel frequencies were blocked;<ref name="Rogue One" /> the Shield Gate was jamming communications.<ref name="Novel">[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story (novelization)|''Rogue One: A Star Wars Story'' novelization]]</ref> Raddus turned around to inform him to keep trying, and the admiral ordered his aide to engage the [[Imperial I-class Star Destroyer|''Imperial I''-class Star Destroyers]] and begin probing the shield.<ref name="Rogue One" />

As rebel forces were lost in the battle, Shollan informed Raddus that they were having no effect on the Shield Gate and were sustaining heavy losses, which the admiral affirmed. When the [[BTL-A4 Y-wing assault starfighter/bomber|Y-wing starfighters]] of [[Gold Squadron (Rebel Alliance)|Gold Squadron]] disabled an [[Persecutor|''Imperial''-class Star Destroyer]], Shollan called out that the [[Imperial-class Star Destroyer|destroyer]] had lost power.<ref name="Novel" />

===Receving the plans===
{{Quote|Admiral, receiving transmission from Scarif!|Shollan|audio=Shollan-Transmission.flac|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
[[File:ReceivingTransmission-RO.png|thumb|left|300px|Shollan informs Raddus of the transmission.]]
Just then, former Imperial [[pilot]] [[Bodhi Rook]], who was on Scarif, tried to contact the rebel fleet to inform them that they would have to break open the Shield Gate in order to transmit the [[Death Star]] plans. He reached the ''Profundity'', and Raddus confirmed to Rook that they heard him as Shollan listened. Rook explained that Erso and [[Captain]] [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]] had found the Death Star plans but needed the Shield Gate down to transmit them, so Raddus ordered Shollan and the other rebels behind him to call up a [[Sphyrna-class Hammerhead corvette|''Sphyrna''-class Hammerhead corvette]]. The [[Lightmaker|corvette]] successfully knocked one [[Star Destroyer]] into the [[Intimidator|other]], causing both of them to fall to the planet's surface and destroy the Shield Gate. Shollan stood up in his place as the plans were beamed to the ''Profundity'', excitedly informing Raddus that they were receiving a transmission from Scarif.<ref name="Rogue One" /> Raddus ordered him to check the data, and once he did so, he eagerly told the Admiral that they had the plans.<ref name="Novel" />

However, the Death Star whose plans they had retrieved then emerged from hyperspace, and Shollan and Caitken stood up on the [[Bridge (starship)|bridge]] to look at it.<ref name="Rogue One" /> Shollan called out to Raddus that there was a massive energy buildup in the [[battle station]], but the admiral cut him off.<ref name="Novel" /> The station targeted the [[Imperial Center of Military Research|Imperial security complex]] below, where Rogue One was trapped. Shollan, Raddus, and Caitken watched as the complex and surrounding area was destroyed. After a moment of silence, Raddus ordered all craft to jump to hyperspace; many ships did so successfully, but the ''Profundity'' was then disabled by an arriving [[Devastator|Star Destroyer]]<ref name="Rogue One" /> and destroyed,<ref name="TLJ">''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: Incredible Cross-Sections]]''</ref> with Raddus and all his subordinates perishing.<ref name="Encyclopedia">{{EncyclopediaCite|The Rebel Alliance}}</ref>

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|Engage those Star Destroyers and let's start probing that shield!''"<br />"''Yes, sir!|Raddus and Shollan|audio=Raddus-Shollan-Probing.flac|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
Shollan, along with Raddus and Caitken, was eager to pay back the Empire for what they did to the Mon Calamari.<ref name="Topps" /> He and Caitken promised to Raddus their all.<ref name="Caitken Topps">{{Topps|set=2018 Topps Star Wars Galactic Files|cardname=Caitken|link=https://www.tcdb.com/ViewCard.cfm/sid/170092/cid/11644215/2018-Topps-Star-Wars-Galactic-Files-RO22-Caitken}}</ref> Shollan was a Mon Calamari<ref name="Rogue One" /> [[Gender|male]]<ref name="Novel" /> with [[Color|gray]] eyes<ref name="Rogue One" /> and [[Albinism|albino]], white skin.<ref name="ew" /> Due to his hailing from the colder regions of Mon Cala, his [[blood]] was said to have been especially thick.<ref name="UVG" />

==Skills and abilities==
Shollan was efficient in following Raddus's orders.<ref name="UVG" /> He was highly intelligent and had advanced [[diplomat]]ic skills, along with average speed, strength, and fighting ability. He was not [[Force-sensitive]].<ref name="Topps" />

==Equipment==
He wore a dark, gray [[Clothing|uniform]] with blue sleeves and a black [[belt]].<ref name="Rogue One" /> He also carried a [[datapad]].<ref name="UVG" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|I said to fans at the time, they are going to want a younger guy who can do it not an old man who needs to go for a pee. That actually did happen in Rogue One&hellip;I was Shollan in that one. We had gone for six hours solid without a pause break, and my character held up his claw and said, 'I'm sorry but the old man has to pee,' and at that point we got a break.|Tim Rose|<ref name="Pee">{{WebCite|url=https://theirstarwarsstories.com/2020/05/27/tim-rose-his-star-wars-story|text=Tim Rose &ndash; His Star Wars Story|author=Davis, Peter|work=[https://theirstarwarsstories.com Their Star Wars Stories]|archivedate=20210524021648}}</ref>}}
[[File:ShollanCaitkenBTS.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Shollan and Caitken on the set of ''Rogue One'']]
Shollan was created for the [[Star Wars Anthology Series|anthology]] film ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]'',<ref name="Rogue One" /> released [[December 16]], [[2016]],<ref name="Dec 16">{{SW|url=news/why-we-already-love-jyn-erso|text=Why We Already Love Jyn Erso|nolive=1}}</ref> where he was portrayed by [[Tim Rose]],<ref name="Tim">{{Topps|set=2017 Topps Star Wars: Rogue One Series 2|cardname=Tim Rose as Shollan|link=https://www.viciousfun.com/product/topps-star-wars-rogue-one-tim-rose-as-shollan-signed-card}}</ref> a puppeteer who portrayed another Mon Calamari, Admiral [[Gial Ackbar]], in the [[1983]] [[original trilogy]] film, [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']].<ref name="Episode VI">{{Film|VI}}</ref> Rose was credited as a creature puppeteer.<ref name="Rogue One" /> At one point during the production of ''Rogue One'', after filming for six hours without taking a break, Rose held up one of Shollan's [[Limb|hands]] to indicate that he needed to take a break to use the bathroom, which he was then granted.<ref name="Pee" /> Shollan and Caitken's designs were reminiscent of Mon Calamari [[Admiral]] [[Gial Ackbar]] from the [[1983]] [[original trilogy]] film {{Film|VI}}, albeit in a different color, while Raddus was more of a new Mon Cal look.<ref name="Moviemaking">''[[The Moviemaking Magic of Star Wars: Creatures & Aliens]]''</ref>

Footage of Shollan was first showcased in a reel of ''Rogue One'' footage revealed at [[Celebration Europe (2016)|Celebration Europe]] on [[July 15]] of that year.<ref name="SW">{{SWYouTube|HUb_zpdyDpU|Rogue One: A Star Wars Story - Celebration Reel|sw_url=video/rogue-one-a-star-wars-story-celebration-reel}}</ref> Shollan was identified in the accompanying reference book to ''Rogue One'', ''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]'',<ref name="UVG" /> published the same day as the film.<ref name="NYCC">{{SW|url=news/rogue-one-and-star-wars-40th-publishing-programs-revealed|text=NYCC 2016: ''Rogue One'' and ''Star Wars'' 40th Anniversary Publishing Programs Revealed}}</ref> The coloring book ''[[Art of Coloring: Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]'',<ref name="Art" /> published on [[December 20]] of that year,<ref name="NYCC" /> confirmed that Shollan is the Mon Calamari referred to as "lieutenant" in the film.<ref name="Art" />

The [[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story (novelization)|novelization]] for ''Rogue One'' by [[Alexander Freed]] mistakenly attributes the line "Sir! Enemy fighters coming in!" to Shollan,<ref name="Novel" /> while the film shows Caitken saying it.<ref name="Rogue One" />

